  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that (Z)-7-Hydroxynuciferol may interact with KB through a series of target relationships mediated by Cocosamide B. Specifically, (Z)-7-Hydroxynuciferol is predicted to act as a target of Cocosamide B, which in turn targets KB. This pathway is supported by multiple evidence scores, with the highest confidence in the first path, which links (Z)-7-Hydroxynuciferol directly to KB via VMRC-LCP and Cocosamide B. However, the second path, which connects (Z)-7-Hydroxynuciferol to Hepatocyte and then to KB, provides an alternative route, indicating that the interaction may involve multiple intermediate targets. The third path, linking (Z)-7-Hydroxynuciferol to VMRC-LCP and then to Calenduloside C, which targets KB, further supports the involvement of different pathways. These findings collectively suggest that (Z)-7-Hydroxynuciferol may have a role in modulating KB through various molecular mechanisms, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
